1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,586
Before a Zone business releases a withdrawal batch,

2
00:00:03,636 --> 00:00:08,132
an auditor or settlement counterparty may need to check it.

3
00:00:08,182 --> 00:00:13,132
But the operator holds the private ledger and the batch witness.

4
00:00:13,182 --> 00:00:19,950
Sworn creates independently verifiable, audit-ready evidence for that exact batch, without exposing customer transaction contents.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,382
The operator selects the batch in Sworn's local console and starts a proof job.

6
00:00:26,432 --> 00:00:31,436
Sworn runs Tempo's own Zone verification code in a zero-knowledge VM,

7
00:00:31,486 --> 00:00:36,950
then creates proof evidence that a third party can verify on chain.

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,558
On Moderato, our own one-operator Zone, not a Tempo-created one,

9
00:00:41,608 --> 00:00:48,470
settles a batch only after Sworn's proof passes; only then can a withdrawal be paid.

10
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:51,695
Three batches, proven and checked on chain.

11
00:00:51,745 --> 00:00:56,764
A forged batch, even signed by our own sequencer, is rejected.

12
00:00:56,814 --> 00:01:00,450
Anchor to payout: fifty-eight minutes, on one laptop.

13
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:07,818
Go-to-market: one Zone business supplies its witness; we prove one batch and its reviewer re-verifies it.

14
00:01:07,868 --> 00:01:14,726
If it asks for the next batch or upgrade, that is a Proof Operations contract.

15
00:01:14,776 --> 00:01:17,950
That is our go-to-market test — not traction.

16
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,143
ZK proving for Zones is still unimplemented.

17
00:01:21,193 --> 00:01:27,985
Sworn runs Tempo's code, binds to portal-shaped inputs, and is built to track execution upgrades.

18
00:01:28,035 --> 00:01:33,003
The market is not proven — Tempo's Zones have one effective operator.

19
00:01:33,053 --> 00:01:37,108
I work on Reth and Revm, teach that stack,

20
00:01:37,158 --> 00:01:43,950
won a Uniswap Foundation prize at ETHGlobal Tokyo, and spent fifteen years building banking systems.

21
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:45,343
Today: testnet, unaudited.

22
00:01:45,393 --> 00:01:46,736
No customer claimed.

23
00:01:46,786 --> 00:01:54,164
Next, a design partner supplies a batch and decides if independent proof is worth paying for.

24
00:01:54,214 --> 00:01:56,950
Sworn: audit-ready evidence for private execution.
